INT. ORBITAL GREENHOUSE RING - CONTINUOUS

A curved corridor of hydroponic racks, lit violet. Vines trail from brackets. Condensation drips from the ceiling in slow, floating beads.

CAPTAIN ISADORA QUILL (50s, severe, silver crop) grips a handrail. Behind her, DR. HIRO TANABE (40s, lab coat), ENSIGN PELL OKONKWO (20s), and the ring's botanist, MARIGOLD SENN (30s, soil-stained gloves), crowd the hatch. At the far end, the old engineer BARNABY CROSS (60s) and a maintenance bot, UNIT SEVEN, stand beside a red warning light.

ISADORA
Status.

HIRO
Spore bloom in Racks Four through Nine --

MARIGOLD
It's not a bloom, it's a --

PELL
Captain, the seal on Nine is --

ISADORA
One at a time!

BARNABY
Seal's gone. Nine's venting.

UNIT SEVEN
(synthetic)
Atmospheric loss at six percent and climbing.

HIRO
We have minutes.

MARIGOLD
Less if the roots reach the coolant.

PELL
Then we cut Nine loose!

ISADORA
Do it.

Barnaby slams a lever. The red light dies. Everyone exhales together.
